{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1903 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d2eb4063d0c42be4becea7b0b95faabd5c9c6a112a766c3d56a4b031d24d396a" :edb/db-before-t 1902 :edb/db-after-t 1903 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535215 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:45:08.038Z" 13194139535215 true] [17592186192629 1020 #edb/ref 17592186337993 13194139535215 true] [17592186192629 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338000 13194139535215 true] [17592186192629 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338007 13194139535215 true] [17592186192630 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338014 13194139535215 true] [17592186192630 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338018 13194139535215 true] [17592186337993 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337994 13194139535215 true] [17592186337993 1089 "q-162346" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535215 true] [17592186337993 1100 "Let $z$ and $w$ be $4$th roots of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${w}^{4}+1=1$\n- ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1$\n- $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337993 1113 #uuid "42e88d65-fbab-581f-93da-db30051fb9eb" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337993 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ and $w$ are $4$th roots of unity, then (by definition) we have that \n\n$$\n{z}^{4}={w}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n{w}^{4}+1=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4} & =\\frac{{z}^{4}}{{w}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that ${(\\frac{z}{w})}^{4}=1,$ which means that $\\frac{z}{w}$ is a $4$th root of unity. \n\nIn general, the quotient of $n$th roots of unity is an $n$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337995 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337996 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337997 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337998 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337999 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1041 "selection" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337995 13194139535215 true] [17592186337994 1110 #uuid "3a7ac790-6055-5386-ad1b-97fce7090478" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337995 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186337995 1111 #uuid "1d01d7e2-2da1-5c2f-9a50-0c74f9e98908" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337996 1034 "I only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186337996 1111 #uuid "097e2c7f-d1e3-51f5-b6fd-2493c4518988" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337997 1034 "III only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186337997 1111 #uuid "d396d329-9e0b-5b3a-9925-b81a2a8c105c" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337998 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186337998 1111 #uuid "7282e12a-d88e-5401-a1f9-41c022787694" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337999 1034 "II only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186337999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186337999 1111 #uuid "6a63e5a4-1602-5e58-b7f4-97d1804e6d78" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338000 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338001 13194139535215 true] [17592186338000 1089 "q-162347" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338000 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535215 true] [17592186338000 1100 "Let $z$ be a $6$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $({z}^{3})^{2}=-1$\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity\n- ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338000 1113 #uuid "f9d7e6b0-7d90-531b-9d90-fe4de4fcbb33" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338000 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{2}={z}^{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({z}^{3})^{6} & =({z}^{6})^{3} \\\\  & =(1)^{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a $6$th root of unity.\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement I, we have that \n\n$$\n({z}^{3})^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nThis means that (by definition) ${z}^{3}$ is a square root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338002 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338003 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338004 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338005 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338006 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1041 "selection" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338002 13194139535215 true] [17592186338001 1110 #uuid "a6ded73b-7a61-5d96-a812-544e399a0958" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338002 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338002 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338002 1111 #uuid "07099299-dbcf-5ce6-b676-1c1c69d969b2" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338003 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338003 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338003 1111 #uuid "631452f4-531e-5022-8057-c343bd82b010" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338004 1034 "III only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338004 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338004 1111 #uuid "b7d5bb98-d00f-5747-8a9d-0a691ffda7c6" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338005 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338005 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338005 1111 #uuid "2075c61a-af42-504f-b1d6-6894d3eaa350" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338006 1034 "II only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338006 1111 #uuid "5321a4d9-764a-5f8a-899e-af4eb02fcd4e" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338007 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338008 13194139535215 true] [17592186338007 1089 "q-162368" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338007 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535215 true] [17592186338007 1100 "Let $z$ be a $4$th root of unity. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${z}^{4}=-1$\n- $(z+z)^{4}=16$\n- $z+z=2z$  is not a $4$th root of unity" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338007 1113 #uuid "9dad6de4-e17a-5465-968b-8caa846ddbf0" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338007 1145 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. If $z$ is a  $4$th root of unity, then (by definition) we have that\n\n$$\n{z}^{4}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z+z)^{4} & =(2z)^{4} \\\\  & ={2}^{4}\\cdot {z}^{4} \\\\  & =16\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. From statement II, we have that $(z+z)^{4}\\ne 1,$ which means that $z+z=2z$ is *not* a $4$th root of unity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338009 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338010 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338011 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338012 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338013 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1041 "selection" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338009 13194139535215 true] [17592186338008 1110 #uuid "a00a1d5a-8491-5e4d-a618-6298b0c3eb69" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338009 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338009 1111 #uuid "295335a8-40fa-5779-9412-21e787238a43" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338010 1034 "I only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338010 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338010 1111 #uuid "acb82636-e366-59ef-99cb-8dc79db7050a" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338011 1034 "III only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338011 1111 #uuid "e0aff68f-d033-5475-b4f1-9e1b9172b684" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338012 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338012 1111 #uuid "b3c66051-46b1-579c-af4f-fc9d1561a2fc" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338013 1034 "II only" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535215 true] [17592186338013 1111 #uuid "534cf28a-4abf-5838-bd60-312b078838f4" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338014 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338015 13194139535215 true] [17592186338014 1089 "q-281256" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338014 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535215 true] [17592186338014 1100 "The sum of all nine $9$th roots of unity is equal to$\\,$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535215 true] [17592186338014 1113 #uuid "5f1224ec-2096-50c1-bcbf-26b6ed16be6f" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338014 1145 "Recall that the principal $9$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/9}\\ne 1,\n$$\n\nand that any $9$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,...,8.$  Also, we have ${z}^{9}=1.$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of a geometric sequence, we obtain that the sum of all eight roots is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+z+{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}+{z}^{4}+{z}^{5}+{z}^{6}+{z}^{7}+{z}^{8} & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-{z}^{9})}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-1)}{1-z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0}{1-z} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338016 13194139535215 true] [17592186338015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338017 13194139535215 true] [17592186338015 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535215 true] [17592186338015 1041 "field-1" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338015 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338017 13194139535215 true] [17592186338015 1110 #uuid "51495358-7bce-59cd-99d3-72eff9c94383" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338016 1034 "9" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535215 true] [17592186338016 1111 #uuid "40e03463-6ce1-5179-8c8e-4b6b3adfcf2f" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338017 1034 "0" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535215 true] [17592186338017 1111 #uuid "0d7c5f42-6bc1-5cad-8aca-db63f5578062" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338018 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338019 13194139535215 true] [17592186338018 1089 "q-319771" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338018 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535215 true] [17592186338018 1100 "The product of all sixteen $16$th roots of unity is equal to$\\,$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535215 true] [17592186338018 1113 #uuid "15d26d14-a520-55b9-aaa0-7122add2005f" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338018 1145 "Recall that the principal $16$th root of unity is \n\n$$\nz={e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/16}={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/8},\n$$\n\nand that any $16$th root of unity is of the form ${z}^{k}$ for $k=0,1,...,15.$ Also, we have ${z}^{16}=1.$\n\nTherefore, the product of all sixteen roots is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{0}\\cdot {z}^{1}\\cdot {z}^{2}\\cdot {z}^{3}\\cdot {z}^{4}\\cdot {z}^{5}\\cdot {z}^{6}\\cdot {z}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{8}\\cdot {z}^{9}\\cdot {z}^{10}\\cdot {z}^{11}\\cdot {z}^{12}\\cdot {z}^{13}\\cdot {z}^{14}\\cdot {z}^{15} & ={z}^{0\\,+\\,1\\,+\\,2\\,+\\,3\\,+\\,4\\,+\\,5\\,+\\,6+\\,⋯+15} \\\\  & ={z}^{120} \\\\  & ={z}^{112+8} \\\\  & ={z}^{112}\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & ={({z}^{16})}^{7}\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & =1\\cdot {z}^{8} \\\\  & ={z}^{8} \\\\  & ={({e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/8})}^{8} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi \\text{i}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338019 1000 #edb/ref 17592186338020 13194139535215 true] [17592186338019 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535215 true] [17592186338019 1041 "field-1" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338019 1104 #edb/ref 17592186338020 13194139535215 true] [17592186338019 1110 #uuid "21438280-2aa9-5a48-bf4f-edf4e775a007" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338020 1034 "-1" 13194139535215 true] [17592186338020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535215 true] [17592186338020 1111 #uuid "78be4c2e-1eee-598b-a22c-b75c5d0c61f2" 13194139535215 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-162346" 17592186337993 "q-162346/selection" 17592186337994 "q-162346/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" 17592186337995 "q-162346/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" 17592186337996 "q-162346/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" 17592186337997 "q-162346/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" 17592186337998 "q-162346/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" 17592186337999 "q-162347" 17592186338000 "q-162347/selection" 17592186338001 "q-162347/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" 17592186338002 "q-162347/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" 17592186338003 "q-162347/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" 17592186338004 "q-162347/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" 17592186338005 "q-162347/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" 17592186338006 "q-162368" 17592186338007 "q-162368/selection" 17592186338008 "q-162368/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" 17592186338009 "q-162368/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" 17592186338010 "q-162368/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" 17592186338011 "q-162368/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f7355857605214